{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":266061,"duration_api_ms":192667,"ttft_ms":1716,"ttft_stream_ms":1716,"time_to_request_ms":257,"num_turns":30,"result":"Iteration complete. Summary:\n\n**exp002 — coverage-first (in-schema over-generate sweep)**\n\n- **Hypothesis** (grounded in exp001 per-case notes): precision was already 1.0 everywhere; the entire residual was *under-extraction* on interleaved multi-task rambles (`interleaved_deck` 2/3, `multi_errands` 2/3, `long_monday` 5/6, coverage rubric 2–3). I added a `candidateIntentions` field forcing an exhaustive whole-input sweep before the deduped `tasks`, keeping the zero-task gate intact.\n- **Build:** green.\n- **Result:** **QUALITY 0.943** vs exp001 **0.955** — a –0.012 delta, within noise, **not a win → discarded**.\n- **Honest read:** the sweep is a real trade, not a fix. It recovered the buried task in `multi_errands` (0.8→1.0) but the over-listing made `dedup_groceries` emit a duplicate (precision 1.0→0.955), and `interleaved_deck` still dropped its prerequisite. Pushing recall via in-schema over-listing costs dedup precision; net wash.\n- **Forward signal logged:** recall gains likely need a dedup pass that structurally can't leak duplicates (e.g. a scoped merge/critique stage), rather than relying on the same call to both over-list and dedup.\n\nExactly one new config (`exp002`), one logged run (`kept: false`), green build. Stopping.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5f166e88-dbf9-4dd4-af6d-d6a9c74d936e","total_cost_usd":0.7826784999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":58,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30914,"cache_read_input_tokens":553034,"output_tokens":12484,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":30914},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":507,"cache_read_input_tokens":30454,"cache_creat