{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":273040,"duration_api_ms":198090,"ttft_ms":1610,"ttft_stream_ms":1609,"time_to_request_ms":249,"num_turns":27,"result":"Iteration complete. One experiment, green build, one new logged run.\n\n## Summary\n\n**exp003 — extract→coverage-audit (2-call pipeline)** — DEV quality **0.931**, **DISCARDED** (−0.024 vs exp001's 0.955).\n\n**Hypothesis:** exp001's entire residual loss was pure *recall* on three multi-task cases (dropped buried/prerequisite tasks), with precision a perfect 1.0. I added a second scoped call that sees the committed task list and adds *only* genuinely-missing stated tasks — skipped entirely when the base list is empty (protecting the solved zero-task gate), with a deterministic dedup safety net.\n\n**Result — honest read:** The recall lever genuinely works on the hardest interleaved inputs (`multi_errands` 0.8→1.0; `interleaved_deck` recovered its Q3-numbers prerequisite → judged a tie; recall rose 0.924→0.985). But it **over-fired on single-task cases**, re-emitting a paraphrased/deadline-qualified variant of the lone task even with the list visible (`dedup_groceries` and `mixed_weekend` each gained a duplicate; precision 1.0→0.909). String dedup can't catch paraphrase duplicates. This is the same precision↔recall tension that sank exp002 — the recall gain on hard cases is exactly cancelled by precision loss on easy ones.\n\n**exp001 remains best.** Logged a clear next lever: gate the audit to multi-task contexts only, or tighten its add-criterion to require a verb/object absent from every listed item.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"bad1bc8b-f363-46d8-a022-012377280d35","total_cost_usd":0.7888012499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":52,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31919,"cache_read_input_tokens":553527,"output_tokens":12469,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":31919},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":538,"cache_read_input_tokens":32646,"cache_creation_input_tokens":657,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":657,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":52,"outputTokens":12469,"cacheReadInputTokens":553527,"cacheCreationInputTokens":31919,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7882422499999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"be32c474-353a-4c82-ba33-5671ebcb942d"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":211814,"duration_api_ms":139175,"ttft_ms":1587,"ttft_stream_ms":1586,"time_to_request_ms":148,"num_turns":20,"result":"Iteration complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Hypothesis** (grounded in the exp003 log's explicit next-step recommendation): exp001's only losses are all **recall on multi-task cases** with precision pinned at 1.0. exp003's recovery audit fixed those but regressed two **single-task** cases by re-adding paraphrase duplicates. So: gate the audit to fire only when the base extraction already found ≥2 tasks.\n\n**Implementation** (exp004, `extractAuditGated`): added a `minBaseTasks: Int = 2` threshold to the existing `extractAudit` topology — single-task inputs skip the audit entirely and keep exp001's behavior; multi-task inputs get the recall recovery. No prompt/schema changes, minimal surgical diff.\n\n**Result — green build, one new logged run:**\n- **QUALITY 0.992** (kept: true, new dev best), up +0.037 from exp001's 0.955.\n- interleaved_deck 0.80→1.00 and multi_errands 0.80→1.00 (the two predicted recall recoveries).\n- dedup_groceries and mixed_weekend stayed at 1.00 (audit correctly skipped — base.count=1).\n- Precision held 1.0; recall 0.924→0.985.\n\n**Brutally honest caveat I logged:** +0.037 sits *under* the single-case noise floor (~0.09). The win is not a wiggle — it's two distinct, judge-confirmed multi-task recall recoveries with zero precision cost — but it's modest, so whether it holds on the held-out TEST split (run automatically by the wrapper) is the real test. Residual headroom: long_monday still 0.91 (the buried insurance-call task among 6 wasn't recovered).","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0ca727fb-b44a-4a0c-911d-11f059fbd821","total_cost_usd":0.5765920000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30296,"cache_read_input_tokens":341646,"output_tokens":8628,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":30296},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":585,"cache_read_input_tokens":31166,"cache_creation_input_tokens":514,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":514,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":32,"outputTokens":8628,"cacheReadInputTokens":341646,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30296,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5760330000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"2642ea85-101a-4f8d-9254-04d9daecfc9e"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":220865,"duration_api_ms":153677,"ttft_ms":1848,"ttft_stream_ms":1846,"time_to_request_ms":217,"num_turns":17,"result":"Iteration complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Experiment exp005** — `extractAuditSweep`: gated audit (base≥2) that ENUMERATES every action in the input (hedged ones included) then DIFFS against the committed list.\n\n- **Hypothesis:** exp004's only residual failure (`long_monday` 0.909) was a softly-hedged, buried task (\"probably call the insurance company\") dropped among digressions. Forcing the audit to exhaustively enumerate before diffing should surface it.\n- **Result:** **quality 0.939 — DISCARDED** (−0.053 vs exp004 best 0.992, `kept: false`). Green build, one new logged run.\n- **Why it failed:** the over-generate sweep poisoned the same-call diff. The model re-emitted paraphrased/split duplicates of items it had just listed — `multi_errands` 1.0→0.67 (split \"call dentist to reschedule\" into two and dropped the quarterly report), `multi_moving` 1.0→0.83 (triplicated \"pack kitchen\", and my literal schema example words \"maybe\"/\"eventually\" leaked into outputs). Precision fell 1.0→0.929. And it *still* missed the insurance call.\n- **Honest signal / lesson:** a louder audit is the wrong lever — an over-generate sweep needs a dedup the model can actually enforce, which a same-call diff field can't. The hedged-buried task is dropped at **base extraction**, not just the audit, so recovery must happen earlier in the pipeline. exp004 (0.992) remains the best. Also a concrete reminder: example phrases in `@Guide` descriptions can leak verbatim into outputs — keep schema examples abstract.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"da705f5a-4baa-4891-8458-3fa19222c5f9","total_cost_usd":0.6383929999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":30,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35018,"cache_read_input_tokens":346443,"output_tokens":9824,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":35018},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":571,"cache_read_input_tokens":35000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1402,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1402,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":30,"outputTokens":9824,"cacheReadInputTokens":346443,"cacheCreationInputTokens":35018,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6378339999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"7c8762e1-c17c-4960-a6ea-a3d5ffc580a7"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":294180,"duration_api_ms":184802,"ttft_ms":1542,"ttft_stream_ms":1541,"time_to_request_ms":148,"num_turns":24,"result":"Iteration complete. Summary of this experiment:\n\n## exp007 — phrasing/style contract on the exp002 coverage topology\n\n**Hypothesis (grounded in the per-case judge notes):** every prior config scored phrasing 2/5 — the dominant, unsaturated gap. Every notes line complained of \"terse all-lowercase fragments that drop meaningful detail.\" I added an explicit STYLE contract (capitalize, complete imperative one-liners, keep purpose/recipient/subject/deadline, drop only vague filler timing) to both the prompt and the final-tasks `@Guide`, on top of the current-best `singleShotCoverage` topology.\n\n**Result: DISCARDED.** Quality **0.812 vs exp002 0.892** (−0.080).\n\n**Honest read of the signal — this was actually informative:**\n- The phrasing lever *works*: rubric phrasing jumped **2→4** (mean), and the easy cases now read like Sonnet (mixed_gym, mixed_weekend, multi_moving, noisy_filler all tie SET A on style).\n- But folding style into the *same* extraction call **poisoned recall**: F1 0.963→0.829. interleaved_party collapsed 3→1 tasks, long_monday lost two, and single_paris + noisy_selfcorrect (both 1.0 in exp002) dropped to F1 0.00. The heavier prompt shifted the greedy decode — the model spent capacity styling instead of extracting.\n\n**Lesson logged for the next iteration:** phrasing is a real, winnable lever, but it must be **decoupled from extraction** — applied as a style-only rewrite pass over the already-extracted list (which cannot change set membership / F1), not as instructions inside the extractor.\n\nBuild is green; exactly one new logged run (`exp007`, kept: false). All prior configs intact.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3781a022-0e48-4c9d-8975-141bf433444e","total_cost_usd":0.9069665000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":42,"cache_creation_input_tokens":44750,"cache_read_input_tokens":589120,"output_tokens":13278,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":44750},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":619,"cache_read_input_tokens":43714,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1036,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":42,"outputTokens":13278,"cacheReadInputTokens":589120,"cacheCreationInputTokens":44750,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9064075000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"fc27a470-24c8-49e2-9906-387d3a6d010e"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":301457,"duration_api_ms":171718,"ttft_ms":1637,"ttft_stream_ms":1636,"time_to_request_ms":150,"num_turns":22,"result":"Iteration complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Hypothesis (grounded in the exp007 log):** Phrasing is a real, winnable lever — exp007 lifted rubric phrasing 2→4 in isolation but poisoned recall by bundling style into the extraction call. The log prescribed: keep the exp002 base unchanged, then apply phrasing as a **decoupled style-only rewrite pass** that \"cannot change set membership.\"\n\n**What I built (exp008 `singleShotCoverageRestyle`):** Call 1 = the proven exp002 extractor, unchanged. Call 2 rewrites each extracted task 1:1 into Sonnet's capitalized/complete style, restoring detail from the input, with a deterministic count/order guard mapping index-wise (count mismatch → keep base).\n\n**Result: DEV quality 0.826 vs exp002's 0.892 — REGRESSED by −0.066, DISCARDED.**\n\n**Why it failed (the honest, useful signal):**\n1. **\"Restore the meaningful detail\" induced hallucination.** Told to recover dropped detail, the model invented plausible-but-absent specifics: \"grab some milk\" → \"Sarah / 3 PM / milk supplier / delivery shipment\" (F1 → ~0); \"Dr. Smith / for the meeting\"; padded rationale like \"to save money / for my new home.\"\n2. **The 1:1 count guard does NOT protect F1.** It preserves cardinality, but semantic drift *within* a slot rewrites a task into a different one — paraphrase set-match still breaks (F1 0.963→0.870). My core assumption that \"same count ⇒ same F1\" was wrong.\n3. **Phrasing rubric didn't even rise** (stayed at 3) — the hallucinated padding reads as \"editorialized,\" not Sonnet style.\n\n**Logged insight / next direction:** \"restore detail\" is the wrong instruction. The phrasing lever must improve case/completeness **without adding content** — e.g. a near-deterministic rewrite constrained so its tokens are a subset of input∪base (no free generation), or a hard \"add no word not present in the input or the task\" constraint. exp004 (0.992) remains the standing best to build on.\n\nBuild is green; exactly one new run (exp008) logged.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"bf486dd5-c165-451a-91d5-0fcea985df3c","total_cost_usd":0.813375,"usage":{"input_tokens":36,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42914,"cache_read_input_tokens":519847,"output_tokens":11380,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":42914},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":790,"cache_read_input_tokens":43419,"cache_creation_input_tokens":879,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":879,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":36,"outputTokens":11380,"cacheReadInputTokens":519847,"cacheCreationInputTokens":42914,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.812816,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"8926a994-a32d-4576-adcf-cf6e324ad849"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":306187,"duration_api_ms":177199,"ttft_ms":1849,"ttft_stream_ms":1841,"time_to_request_ms":163,"num_turns":20,"result":"Done. One iteration complete:\n\n**exp009** — Hardened exp008's decoupled restyle pass with a per-task **token-subset anti-hallucination guard** + deterministic capitalization.\n\n- **Build:** green.\n- **Run:** logged (`results/exp009.json`, run kept).\n- **QUALITY 0.922** (dev) vs exp002's 0.892 best — **new dev best (+0.030)**, though honestly near the noise floor.\n\nWhat it proved: the guard did exactly what the exp008 log prescribed — F1 held at **0.963** (set membership identical to exp002 by construction) and exp008's hallucination is gone (dedup_groceries no longer fabricates \"Sarah/3 PM/milk supplier\"; the guard rejected those novel content words and fell back to the capitalized base). Phrasing rubric lifted 2→3.\n\nBrutally honest caveat: the win is modest and mostly banked **capitalization**, not completeness — the conservative guard suppressed most detail-restoring restyles, so the judge still dings dropped detail (\"about the kitchen sink\", \"before Friday\") and proper-noun casing (\"dana's\"). Logged the next lever: deterministic proper-noun re-casing from the input + investigating why input-present detail restyles get rejected.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3cd45890-0bdb-456d-bf5a-867b0b474047","total_cost_usd":0.8369202499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":45693,"cache_read_input_tokens":505240,"output_tokens":11920,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":45693},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":604,"cache_read_input_tokens":46207,"cache_creation_input_tokens":870,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":870,"ephemeral_1h_input_to